/id #edb/ref 17592186502358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10044cc3-3b39-5d32-a498-68916d941200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502329} {:answer/id #uuid "17c2381b-c4e7-5a02-b1bd-1af3ad2fe815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502336} {:answer/id #uuid "33b225c1-7ac2-59b0-87c8-2d938ed0e64c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502345} {:answer/id #uuid "b3420529-9ac1-56ba-9621-898ba6e04a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502392} {:answer/id #uuid "becfdc1d-6591-5de1-83cf-85a6a6e00bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502400}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502329} :answer-field/id #uuid "431eaaa1-c585-54de-bea0-dfe869377d08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "59ffdb7f-6502-5ff8-b1d6-0cd16904d80b" :question/problem "![](images/42/42b28384b26d180eb7ac4fb945a1e75659961be7a4eae1aaed42abe2c861b3ca.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/93/93cd69372903948a36ea13c7db78c1f2df59db19cdb882089263896d7313432e.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=1$ and $BH=1.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(1)^2+\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{13}}{13}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f51b159-ea75-5a59-8717-0c45b2ed7ce1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{37}}{37}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502328} {:answer/id #uuid "141f8e46-00b6-5edb-9b87-b7642576a28c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{37}}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502331} {:answer/id #uuid "30240caf-a126-530f-b211-a9a6f26c71f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{37}}{37}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502343} {:answer/id #uuid "37821061-f4a7-54a6-ac8e-8ecd87c7dbe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{37}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502347} {:answer/id #uuid "8c256041-15e9-5b30-a73c-055ffa53fb81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502373}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502328} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba5ce94e-e328-592b-a1b0-2e3209c0ac18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "add307e1-eba2-5029-b8ba-35bea556d853" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1dbd27c1b4987c7b6196da934b586f93062d5e9a77144a0c9defb3f8db9adf17.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/e8/e81324960632400a3af894d472f054a9e5035dc77ccf8ce87b6720d5af2d5b2f.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=0.5$ and $BH=3$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2+(3)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+9} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{37}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{37}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{37}}{37}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "175716d6-f724-5abd-89ff-3f8a07a173f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{29}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502335} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf6d763-5cbb-5d44-af46-95fc5c977990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502374} {:answer/id #uuid "98aad0d9-ad4d-522e-a5cb-612dcdbbe2f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{29}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502379} {:answer/id #uuid "c09c9bc4-ee4e-591d-9d2a-f36c3683dbc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502403} {:answer/id #uuid "cd88d19e-3d47-5bbd-adb4-9b532799655f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{58}}{29}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502409}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502335} :answer-field/id #uuid "cead1b10-d18a-5709-b0b2-535c451e4c12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b3b0065f-ddd8-5f3f-97d3-2bf3c18a2472" :question/problem "![](images/da/daa0c47f022b83ba8fe6cd059f7a2971ee92082c9b315f813c93df806b743377.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/ac/ac6e9bcd576c30cd721babe0d12a31cd9a3ba0d4905ad3b02e32d1dd8ca012c9.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=1.5$ and $BH=3.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{49}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{58}}{29}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28bdd9c3-4ba9-5e07-bbc2-23008ea90296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{73}}{73}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502341} {:answer/id #uuid "9410c1d1-61fd-54cf-a43b-724d7c529549" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{73}}{73}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502377} {:answer/id #uuid "c956c0e0-4412-5745-a727-d23da3c13826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502406} {:answer/id #uuid "ca8ceac9-cf04-5c79-81aa-b287c52dda0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502407} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2b09bd-3bb2-5403-ac20-8ab81b1bee5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{73}c" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502427}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502377} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc923f7d-f440-514d-b4d4-6f5c3c87c511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "baa6d129-80bc-5fdf-803e-edf7f11daa38" :question/problem "![](images/02/02112c027add54e9bc7412151f3bd04c31d33e51eb1f96aded05b59e2489950e.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $c$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/d4/d4f6e1f602a4bf57830c11f0814f2fb7d6d1c2304421a32284f6bfb5a92690b5.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=1.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+\\frac{9}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $c$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|c|}\\cdot c \\\\\n&= \\frac{2 \\sqrt{73}}{73}c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502398 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b19e8f3-a552-505b-ad12-58c839a03d63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502360} {:answer/id #uuid "73a6d727-f261-539e-bde2-6afa01192ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502366} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3a0b64-4cf6-5ed7-9627-1b556e84fd08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502380} {:answer/id #uuid "ad475c65-92e0-56bc-a05a-ed7509552376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502384} {:answer/id #uuid "dc00dffb-f2a5-5c41-b487-055ff5e5fad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502415}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502380} :answer-field/id #uuid "707c5601-e0a9-5590-91d2-59bf98a17340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bbfa9f4f-6b90-5698-8173-56c2da86ba47" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b25f39d9bbd30e928d8e07defbed4b2c3e3c4ef46ed92186fb83372dac14b1fd.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/d6/d61b907e6fe5abc9c3e1f3197bfbfc24b7fc67b2e70366877d71d284abf16e85.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=3$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(3)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+9} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $5$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1466a4c6-98a6-5c4f-ae70-75f167118229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502333} {:answer/id #uuid "643d241c-b09e-5d13-be8a-2f780530c24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502361} {:answer/id #uuid "aa33eb03-a7ce-5a51-a4de-b374da32635c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502382} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e4d2ac-8630-5990-b322-df632250a0ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502389} {:answer/id #uuid "ed10a18f-9c1f-56ec-b6f6-99a8b4f36321" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502424}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502424} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b0da6b-7675-58cf-9104-1d77abf27492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "be9bc2f6-f852-5ff9-bd62-113bf0a7214a" :question/problem "![](images/13/1313a6787b3d2da5ddf917ad9cad72791bc465a265dd73cac8fe9c806afc74ec.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/fe/fe7fb47997949a3bbf0699ee771a1a05f8c8d7c6558140719d7f7a00316fc231.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4.5$ and $BH=2.5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{81}{4}+\\frac{25}{4}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{53}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01c33297-8862-52ba-ae7e-117f940f7825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502324} {:answer/id #uuid "096e92bc-d7ac-5de6-9efd-fe57622569d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502327} {:answer/id #uuid "704b4538-66a1-56b4-a0be-0ab16e96992f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502364} {:answer/id #uuid "80148278-4eda-5d27-bc27-3f70e1ec97b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502370} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcd5af2-48b9-5a76-bea9-fec8bca5c287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}(m+n)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502381} :answer-field/id #uuid "905b6f66-d160-5425-bc77-656eb54786d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c065984c-41d2-5c1b-a564-9053a81a79d9" :question/problem "![](images/92/92fcd6bef2b85d707fbe936c7aaa4870b64c158ca12f614123c0957dfa2a0efe.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $m+n$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $m+n$. According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant $m+n$ goes from the tail of $m$ to the head of $n$:\n\n![](images/39/39cc72f1b5da145c6c475c0759ab8df4bead1a136edadfae7c1e17291db451b1.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=1.5$ and $BH=2$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)^2+(2)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $m+n$ is $\\frac{5}{2}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|m+n|}\\cdot (m+n) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{5}(m+n)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050f0936-de36-51aa-be96-34bf22ff255b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502326} {:answer/id #uuid "145c7e10-0411-5226-b0b4-b88138b5fc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502332} {:answer/id #uuid "24708689-ae25-5b89-9e77-19b9b6ff20fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502339} {:answer/id #uuid "3d56e48f-ff61-53aa-ba43-699f7f459463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502350} {:answer/id #uuid "77ace477-261c-5694-b9b7-bf4ec6f695ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502368}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502339} :answer-field/id #uuid "b256d148-8a4a-556c-9fd8-2f409759086c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cb8ba5a3-a4ec-5819-ae01-094d989c17cd" :question/problem "![](images/73/733f3c7b5fde90bb1e33c1988cfc45136c1be0be83464e603ab796128bc6d74c.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/a0/a00c60819288df1d7331b0dcb0f92641378563ef916c3c934e9f11ccade084da.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=2$ and $BH=5$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(5)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4+25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $\\sqrt{29}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{29}}{29}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f25b3c-3cef-58c5-a4a8-107bdf749806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502325} {:answer/id #uuid "3bfaf395-ad67-5305-a35e-e3c34f965fc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502349} {:answer/id #uuid "cea8463b-b2bf-5def-b2df-4b9e0fa7e95a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502410} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d4df14-c44c-5cd0-96cd-0cba8833