17592186502371} {:answer/id #uuid "ae796374-cd08-5e66-8095-8c73e5f88bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502386} {:answer/id #uuid "aeee24af-9b30-5ebe-bc0b-e60e5394d097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{34}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502387}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502371} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ac96a55-9cfd-5fdc-bb84-c6a8f83eb94e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502362}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ddfae147-ff33-5d95-aa67-5f711e17eded" :question/problem "![](images/27/27a852815532c69325ee58633141af9b34215fdb4e53058c8fa0fc3f73e74d37.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f1/f1880e8d87ec11f1199b3283f5eb4dfa32d4794bfc11e40f9239469d98ac5fe3.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=5$ and $BH=3$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(5)^2+(3)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25+9} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{34}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $\\sqrt{34}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{34}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b98bea1-f6d0-569b-a02f-06f7ebfe11bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502338} {:answer/id #uuid "4b64f103-4a0f-5427-abf6-87a5b93eadd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{17}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502353} {:answer/id #uuid "abf39e95-d1db-547f-9fec-5b069d1a6135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502383} {:answer/id #uuid "b178e68c-779a-5054-843e-a75a51bc3a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502388} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e80375-2d4e-5d08-abd4-f6fb022fd894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502353} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cf3e15-cc97-5a13-bd25-8922cfbaabbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd2c3dbb-22ff-5705-a4a4-9ced2ca58d7c" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2a2003ffdc18b5cc19abbe61346906d9ddbe45021109b41e88818d40dd05ee3.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$. Choose the unit vector in the same direction." :question/worked-solution "![](images/23/23a7a8c3471a8f297b1daf5bf52f4314e2360b215083bcb379605801a5984890.png)\n\nIn $\\bigtriangleup AHB$ we have $\\angle AHB=90^\\circ$, $AH=4$ and $BH=1$. So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\sqrt{AH^2+BH^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(1)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16+1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{17}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the magnitude of $a$ is $\\sqrt{17}$. Consequently, the unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{1}{|a|}\\cdot a \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{17}}{17}a\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "184b1119-7733-55a3-841b-a9dd5d48a38e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502439} {:answer/id #uuid "2e8584aa-c4ac-583f-b751-006ec7c797d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{100}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502450} {:answer/id #uuid "348871cc-8723-5bcb-a071-94e01cef9ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502454} {:answer/id #uuid "4b3cb9e5-8269-579f-adaf-280a9a215fee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502467} {:answer/id #uuid "afc3a856-1091-5d4d-87c9-af34e16c977f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502503}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502503} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6967de9-3af5-5bc2-b8c7-9022b2c56f00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "04e0f50e-8727-5a0b-b942-238de6b8a77f" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $6$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $8$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=6^2+8^2\\\\\n&=36+64\\\\\n&=100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{100}=10\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{10}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d470fe8-3276-5fcd-bb6e-0d8a1db6eb01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502448} {:answer/id #uuid "35b0d710-7c12-55ee-923c-df81172318d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{325}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502455} {:answer/id #uuid "e56fb47f-9b33-52a8-8c02-7c3141585692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5 \\sqrt{13}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502523} {:answer/id #uuid "f645117c-8ef3-50bd-837b-8e23b5eee8f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502530} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe939cc-9815-502c-9644-016c40929e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502532}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502523} :answer-field/id #uuid "da27d9c9-7ac2-5d52-93af-f8f1f0dd29d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "15e10e67-a13a-5e2d-88ee-bd7863909bbd" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $\\mid a|= 10$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-east and $\\mid b|= 15$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=10^2+15^2\\\\\n&=100+225\\\\\n&=325\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{325}=5 \\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{5 \\sqrt{13}}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4de5ed72-1b66-5550-8a3b-76c0730e592d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{74}}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502468} {:answer/id #uuid "550c8897-f104-5d26-9018-4248762efd7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502471} {:answer/id #uuid "90b5c3cf-4d0b-520b-a3d4-4e225176f81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502494} {:answer/id #uuid "d46a790e-1e4c-5fec-81cb-de51d204acfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502515} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7dfb77-e690-5d75-bea7-120713797787" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{296}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502518}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502468} :answer-field/id #uuid "54a93966-5147-5736-9afa-6eb0ed2d2ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "16b4c43e-a487-541f-977d-a974199d223a" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed due north-east and $\\mid a|= 10$, while the vector $b$ is directed due south-east and $\\mid b|= 14$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=10^2+14^2\\\\\n&=100+196\\\\\n&=296\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{296}=2 \\sqrt{74}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{74}}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e4de178-e9e0-5843-9dae-4051274aa53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502474} {:answer/id #uuid "72751c45-0a19-5564-b042-f95c5c4c54e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{289}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502479} {:answer/id #uuid "98fcdde1-d05b-5aa0-8906-c38eefd53ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{17}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502496} {:answer/id #uuid "e24f5bf3-8c4b-5d37-8bb6-1245813ce7d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{23}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502521} {:answer/id #uuid "faa42255-4ed0-5f2f-a5d7-71f37714324c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{15}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502531}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502496} :answer-field/id #uuid "0beed4fa-3d81-55c3-a7d1-8ac0221447de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "312b7367-4f56-5bcb-8382-5907780c665c" :question/problem "The vector $a$ is directed horizontally to the right and has magnitude $8$, while the vector $b$ is directed vertically down and has magnitude $15$. Which of the following is a unit vector that is parallel to $a + b$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=8^2+15^2\\\\\n&=64+225\\\\\n&=289\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{289}=17\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{17}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
